module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_type_parameter_resolved_as_an_ordinary_atom_in_v2" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a generic declaration's type parameter reaches v2 resolve with no binder, so `T` is looked up as an ordinary name** (INVALID STATE: the `<T>` list never reached the lowered tree. v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_grammar_generic_params_expr class-stamped the parameter names, so the parse tree carried ^dag_token_ident and not the spelling; v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold treated the list as preserved metadata; the fn Arrow was [domain, codomain, codomain, arrow_body_edge] with no type-parameter edge; and v2.compiler.resolve scoped only VALUE parameters, resolving the domain in the declaration's outer scope. So `T` went through resolve_atom's ordinary chain: lexical frame, symbol index, namespace_has_canonical_symbol.)",
    "HARM, OBSERVED BY EXECUTION on origin/main 57f5b94e7f7 (v2.test.claim.type_param_binder_frame, run by `gunbc run --claim-run` against that tree). Both arms fierce-gull-556 predicted from reading reproduce. `fn f<T>(x: T) -> T { x }` alone REFUSES resolve_reason_unbound_symbol: a true refusal for the wrong reason. The same fn beside `type T = Int` is ACCEPTED with `T` bound to that type: silent wrongness, outside the ladder. Infer had no type variable either: an application of an Arrow whose formal is `x: T` judged `T` as the ordinary declared type and refused an Int argument application_argument_does_not_inhabit. Eight of that witness's rows are red on that main.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. v1's TypeParameterInValuePosition wall (gunbc#12163) is a different class in a different compiler: it refuses a type parameter USED AS A VALUE in the seed, and it presupposes the binder this row says v2 lacked. gunbc.recurring_failure_mode type_variable_means_both_declared_generic_and_inference_variable is v1's meaning fork on InferredNode TypeVariable; v2's model keeps the two apart by construction (v2.std.inhabitance FormalDeclaration has no inference-variable arm) and leaves the v1 row where it is. The recognition rule: a v2-lowered Arrow for a generic declaration with no ^arrow_type_params_edge, or a resolved atom at a type parameter's occurrence that is a refusal or a binding to some other declaration.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-09-24, fierce-gull-556, gunbc#12210 review 70826). Found while lowering `p => body`. The direction chosen for an elided lambda parameter type is a fresh type parameter scoped to the lambda (`<T>(p: T) => body`), and reusing v2's generic-fn representation for it turned up that no such representation existed. First filed as gunbc#12212, closed in favour of the model lane that ships it here.",
    "CLIMB, FN DECLARATIONS (quiet-gull-652). One binder concept in a type role, not a second binder model: the `<T>` names are lexeme-stamped by the same dag_grammar_ident_or_type_decl_modifier_name every declared name uses; body_lower_fn_decl_type_params (now body_lower_decl_type_params) lowers them onto an Arrow type-parameter edge, a Conj of Named binders shaped like the domain, whose well-formedness makes a malformed binder unwritable; v2.compiler.resolve resolve_arrow_node scopes them as a lexical frame over the signature and refuses a parameter that would shadow a visible name (resolve_reason_type_parameter_shadows_visible_name); v2.compiler.infer reads a formal declared as one of the callee's own type parameters as a declared type variable and instantiates it per application. A present-but-unreadable `<...>` refuses body_lowering_reason_type_params_unreadable rather than lowering as if it declared nothing, and the v2 target serializer refuses translate_reason_generic_arrow_not_rendered rather than emitting a signature without its type parameters.",
    "CLIMB, TYPE DECLARATIONS (crisp-dove-95, trigger (1); shape ruled by neat-boar-16: the binder edge on the declaration's member, terminal, not an interim). The binder edge is ONE label for both roles, v2.std.type_binder type_params_marker, a lexeme no source can spell (the v2.std.qualified_name declaration_reference_marker precedent), so a record field or coproduct variant cannot collide with it by construction; the Arrow migrated onto the same label, and v2.std.node keeps only the binder SHAPE (type_binder_conj_conforms) because v2.std.compilers.lexing imports it and it cannot intern the marker. body_lower_type_decl_member carries `<T>` on the member the graft keeps (the record's field Conj, the coproduct's Disj); v2.compiler.resolve resolve_children_homogeneous_scope opens the SAME frame over it through the helpers resolve_arrow_node uses (resolve_type_param_frame, resolve_type_params_conj), so the no-shadowing refusal applies unchanged; v2.compiler.symbol_index_fill skips the edge so `T` is never a declared member `Box.T`. A generic `=` declaration whose right-hand side is not a Conj or Disj (`type Id<T> = T`) has no member to carry the binders and refuses body_lowering_reason_generic_type_decl_member_uncarried rather than dropping them.",
    "RUNG, PER PATH (DESIGN section 4b(1): the class sits at the minimum). Source to resolve for a FN declaration: structurally guaranteed (v2.test.claim.type_param_binder_frame tpb_generic_param_binds_to_its_binder, tpb_type_param_shadowing_a_visible_name_refuses; red on 57f5b94e7f7). Source to resolve for a TYPE declaration (record, coproduct): structurally guaranteed, established by executed evidence -- tpb_type_decl_coproduct_param_binds_to_its_binder, tpb_type_decl_param_shadowing_a_visible_name_refuses, tpb_type_decl_record_keeps_its_type_params, tpb_type_decl_every_param_is_a_binder, all four red on 263f4c00a1d (the colliding coproduct Accepted with `T` bound to `type T = Int`; the bare coproduct and record refused unbound), with a mutation receipt (the member frame removed) that reds the three binding rows. Source to resolve for a generic alias whose rhs is not a member: a typed refusal, fail-closed, the capability absent. Source to v2 emission, fn AND type declaration: a typed refusal at the serializer (tpb_emitter_refuses_a_generic_arrow; tpb_translator_refuses_a_generic_type_decl_member, red with the refusal disabled) -- fail-closed, the capability absent. No path is outside the ladder as measured; the class's current rung is the refusal on the emission paths and the uncarried alias, below the ceiling until triggers (3) and (4).",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a type-position atom refers to a type binder in scope is decidable once the binder is carried in the tree, which it now is for fns.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, each naming a capability. (1) TYPE DECLARATIONS -- DISCHARGED for records and coproducts by the climb above; a generic alias to a non-member rhs still refuses. (2) A BODY TYPE POSITION: the first type position body lowering carries (a `let` annotation, a lambda parameter type) needs a position-aware type frame -- one answering in type positions only -- before the fn's frame may widen from its signature to its body; a frame over the whole body was measured to admit `fn f<T>(x: T) -> T { T }`, a type used as a value. (3) EMISSION: a target grammar row rendering a type-parameter list, replacing the serializer's refusals for fns and type declarations. (4) NESTED AND RETURN INSTANTIATION in infer: v2.std.inhabitance inhabitance_formal_declaration recognizes a type variable only when a formal's WHOLE declared type is the bare binder, so a formal `List<T>` still takes the counted UndecidableGenericFormal frontier (an Instantiation formal), and the declared return type is never instantiated from the arguments; the trigger is instantiation that substitutes through a formal's structure and into the codomain (review 70847). A lambda's own Arrow opens its own frame through resolve_arrow_node, so gunbc#12210's fresh lambda type parameter does not wait on (2).",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.type_binder", decl_name: "type_params_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "type_binder_conj_conforms", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_decl_type_params", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_type_decl_member", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "resolve_arrow_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "resolve_children_homogeneous_scope", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.inhabitance", decl_name: "inhabitance_formal_declaration", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.translate", decl_name: "target_serialize_bodied_arrow_from_model", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.translate", decl_name: "translate_type_expression_project", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.type_param_binder_frame", decl_name: "tpb_type_param_shadowing_a_visible_name_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.type_param_binder_frame", decl_name: "tpb_type_decl_param_shadowing_a_visible_name_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
